results.evidence:
Upon transitioning between the cases below, the UE shall apply the NR sidelink communication related configurations as included in SIB12, if available, or as included in SidelinkPreconfigNR otherwise:
1> RRC_CONNECTED;
1> RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE;
1> Other cases (e.g. out of coverage), using SidelinkPreconfigNR.
The UE shall release the NR sidelink communication related configurations applied for the case in which the UE previously was, upon transitioning between the above cases.

{
  "evidence": "When full configuration is used, the UE releases the MRBs configured for multicast MBS reception. If, after applying the full configuration, the MRB(s) for multicast MBS is (are) configured again by the network, the AS layer treats this as an MRB establishment rather than as a re-establishment/re-setup of a previously released MRB, i.e. the configuration is treated as a new configuration and not as a resumption of the previously suspended/released multicast MRB context (e.g. PDCP state, security context associated with that MRB are not preserved across the full configuration release and subsequent setup).",
  "retrieved_contexts": [
    "TS 38.331 clause 5.3.5.7 Reconfiguration with sync / Full configuration: Upon performing full configuration, the UE releases the current UE configuration including radio bearer configurations, MAC, RLC, PDCP entities, and applies the received full configuration as if it were received in an RRC connection setup, meaning all previous configurations not explicitly included are released and new ones are treated as newly established.",
  ]
}

1> upon selecting a suitable NR cell:
2> stop timer T311;
3> if timer T310 is running:
4> stop timer T310;
2> apply the default L1 parameter values as specified in the corresponding physical layer specification, except for the parameters for which values are provided in SIB1;
2> apply the default MAC Cell Group configuration as specified in 9.2.2;
2> apply the CCCH configuration as specified in 9.1.1.2;
2> apply the timeAlignmentTimerCommon included in SIB1;
2> initiate transmission of the RRCReestablishmentRequest message in accordance with 5.3.7.4.

1> if the sl-ReportType is set to sl-periodical:
2> remove the entry with the matching sl-measId from the VarMeasReportListSL, if any;
2> remove the sl-measId from the sl-MeasIdList within VarMeasConfigSL, if present.

1> else if the physical cell identity of the new serving cell does not match any of the entries in the validityCellList for the serving frequency in the validityAreaList within VarMeasIdleConfig:
2> stop timer T331;
2> clear VarMeasIdleConfig and VarMeasIdleReport, if any;
2> stop any idle/inactive measurements being performed by the UE.

1> if validityAreaList is configured in VarMeasIdleConfig and the serving frequency after cell selection is not equal to the carrierFreq of an entry in validityAreaList:
2> stop timer T331;
2> clear VarMeasIdleReport and VarMeasIdleConfig, if stored;
2> stop any idle/inactive measurements being performed by the UE.

1> if the RRCReconfiguration includes the scg-State with value deactivated:
2> suspend SCG transmission for all SRBs, and if configured, MCG SRB3, and stop the SCG SCells and the PSCell in accordance with 5.3.5.19;
2> not apply the stored scg-RB configuration for the RRCReconfiguration until scg-State is included with the value 'active', or reconfigurationWithSync for the PSCell is received, or until the SCG is released;
2> not apply the measurement configuration associated with the SCG, if any, until the SCG is activated;
2> for each measId included in the measConfig, if any, associated with the SCG, if any, remove the entry with the matching measId from the VarMeasConfig if the SCG was previously in state 'active' and store the received measConfig associated with the SCG;
2> stop timer T310 for the corresponding SCG, if running;
2> stop timer T312 for the corresponding SCG, if running.

1> for each DAPS bearer:
2> release the DAPS bearer configuration for the source SpCell, upon successful completion of the random access procedure towards the target SpCell as specified in TS 38.321;
2> stop the DAPS UL data transmission towards the source SpCell;
2> release the source SCG configuration, if configured;
2> release the source RLC entity and the associated logical channel used for the DAPS bearer towards the source SpCell;
2> reconfigure the PDCP entity to release the DAPS bearer configuration, i.e. to not duplicate PDCP PDUs towards both source and target SpCells;
2> configure the PDCP entity to resume normal PDCP operation for the bearer using the target configuration, i.e. discard the source configuration.
